# Module boundaries

## Simulation (`World`, `world_*.cpp`, `data`, `map`, `ai`)

- May mutate `World` state and use `Rng`.
- Must stay deterministic for a given seed + cmd stream.
- Must **not** include menu/HUD drawing, cursor textures, or Winsock.

## Presentation (`gfx/`, `sfx/`, bake/draw helpers)

- Read `World` / assets; draw or play audio.
- Must **not** invent new win conditions, damage formulas, or production rules.

## App / UI (`game.cpp`, `game_*.cpp` except pure tests)

- Translate input → `World::Cmd` via `issueCmd` / net path.
- Own phases, camera, selection, placement preview, menus.
- Campaign triggers may call into `World` spawn APIs, but combat rules stay in `World`.

## New features

Place code in the existing subsystem file from `docs/architecture.md`. If none fits, **add a new `world_*.cpp` or `game_*.cpp`** rather than appending hundreds of lines to `game.cpp` / `world.cpp`.
